{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511084-the-consecrated-of-vesta-homebrew-proximus-legacy","id":1511084,"title":"The Consecrated of Vesta (Homebrew Proximus Legacy)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-08T14:21:04-07:00","id":1511084,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The Consecrated of Vesta (Homebrew Proximus Legacy)","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Consecrated of Vesta</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The modern day Vestals trace their origins back to the late Roman Republic. A Mage Vestal who wished to truly sanctify her goddess took it upon herself to experiment with making the perfect priestesses; it is this Mage who is behind at least some of the stories of virgin births among the Vestals of yore.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Whether the virgin births, or one of her other many experiments, was the ultimate trigger is irrelevant, modern Vestals exist and are not bound to virginity; in the modern day they work to ensure that homes are safe, people are comfortable and protected, and that neither deceit nor desecration occurs where they can stop it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Not all Vestals are women, but the majority are; and many do still dedicate either a portion or all of their lives to Vesta, though what that looks like in modern nights varies from Vestal to Vestal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Nicknames:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Vestals, Hearth Keepers.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Appearance:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Vestals tend to be homebodies, and are often on the pale side and lacking in marks of prolonged sun exposure (e.g. freckles). When in a good mood the comforting heat of their Hearth radiates from their skin, when angered one could be forgiven for thinking they served Vulcan rather than Vesta.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In death their bodies are consumed by fire. If the death was peaceful the fire causes no harm to the surroundings, if violent a bonfire capable of causing third degree burns is left behind for a number rounds equal to the Vestal\u2019s maximum Willpower.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Parent Path:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Obrimos</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Blessings (Forces, Prime, Life):</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Forces - Influence Fire (\u2022), Influence Heat (\u2022), Control Fire (\u2022\u2022), Environmental Shield (\u2022\u2022), Turn Momentum (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Prime - Pierce Deception (\u2022), Sacred Geometry (\u2022); Supernal Veil (\u2022\u2022), Wards and Signs (\u2022\u2022), Geomancy (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Stealing Fire (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Life - Analyze Life (\u2022), Cleanse the Body (\u2022), Body Control (\u2022\u2022), Purge Illness (\u2022\u2022), Knit (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Curse:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Every Vestal has a hearth to which they must tend, and this hearth must be consecrated to that purpose. Consecrating a hearth takes a Wits + Occult extended action requiring 10 total successes at 1 hour per roll. A temporary hearth can be set up if the Vestal will be away from her primary hearth for more than a day, a temporary hearth requires only 5 successes and the Vestal suffers no penalty if it is desecrated. The desecration of the permanent hearth affects the Vestal even if the Vestal is in a distant land, there is a mystical connection between them. Consecrating a hearth does not take the normal 1 WP/roll for extended actions away from her hearth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Persistent:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Being away from her hearth, even a temporary one, causes the Vestal to become distracted and inattentive, the feeling of having &quot;left the oven on&quot; turned up to 11. The Vestal takes a -2 die penalty on all rolls involving perception, concentration, and precision. Engaging in an extended action costs a point of Willpower per roll.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Beat:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Whenever the Vestal suffers a major setback from failing a perception, concentration, or precision roll or is unable to complete an extended action due to a lack of willpower, take a beat.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Severe:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> if the Vestal suffers a Paradox, their permanent hearth is desecrated, or they go a full day without tending to their hearth (either permanent or temporary) then the Vestal withdraws into herself, going numb to the world. The Vestal cannot take any actions other than dedicating a new hearth, trying to return to her permanent hearth, or fleeing danger. She can still apply Defense to attacks and can spend a Willpower to act normally for a turn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Oblations:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Tending to the hearth. Providing aid and comfort to visitors in her home. Blessing a newly constructed home or a home with new residents.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Character concepts:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Interior designer, housewife/husband, midwife, therapist, counselor.</span></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 05-08-2023, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T20:22:29-07:00","id":1511175,"title":"","content":"A very flavorful Proximi Dynasty, with a very interesting Curse. I am curious on how aware or restrained they are when in &quot;Vestal mode&quot;. If they were captured, would they divulge any information of their allies if they logically thought they would be let go or it would open a chance to escape ? Would they ignore their surroundings to a degree as long as the broad components to dedicate a new/temporary hearth were present ? Would there be a sudden surge of clarity when they return from &quot;autopilot mode&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T15:09:55-07:00","id":1511288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511084-the-consecrated-of-vesta-homebrew-proximus-legacy?p=1511175#post1511175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A very flavorful Proximi Dynasty, with a very interesting Curse. I am curious on how aware or restrained they are when in &quot;Vestal mode&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say they are distracted and unable to focus on anything other than getting to the permanent hearth or consecrating a new permanent hearth.<br /> <br /> An ST might substitute the current effects for something more like Vampire's Frenzy, if a more uncontrolled feel is desired.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they were captured, would they divulge any information of their allies if they logically thought they would be let go or it would open a chance to escape ? </div> </div> </div>Divulging detailed secrets would require an expenditure of a Willpower, complex suppositions such as &quot;maybe I can bargain my way out&quot; are difficult under the effects of the Severe curse. A PC captor might bring it up as Hard Leverage against an NPC Vestal, but I don't think they'd be any more inclined to sell out their friends than anyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would they ignore their surroundings to a degree as long as the broad components to dedicate a new/temporary hearth were present ? </div> </div> </div>I didn't go into detail above, but my general thoughts are they'd need a specific Resonance to dedicate a Hearth, in addition to the rolls, hence the inclusion of <i>Sacred Geometry</i> and <i>Geomancy</i>, thus a hostile location would be unconducive on a mystical level. Either way, though, it does not override their own general sense of self-preservation: escape is always an option even if the location would make a valid Hearth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would there be a sudden surge of clarity when they return from &quot;autopilot mode&quot; ? </div> </div> </div>Probably! Putting off Breaking Points until the Vestal resolved the Severe curse would make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> Thank you for taking a look! I always enjoy your feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}